Font licensing — PARTIALLY RESOLVED (2026-07-30)
================================================

RESOLVED: font-dejavu. Its full Bitstream Vera / Arev notice now ships as LICENSE.dejavu in
this directory, extracted VERBATIM from the fonts' own OpenType name table (record 13) rather
than transcribed from a website — that is the text the binaries we redistribute actually carry.
Both faces are reproduced because they differ: DejaVuSans-Bold includes an Arev-glyphs clause
that DejaVuSansMono does not, so shipping one notice would drop a clause covering the other.

STILL OUTSTANDING: font-unifont. Its pack ships only a two-line README (name + URL) and its
TTF carries NO licence record at all, so there is nothing on disk to extract. GPL-2 is present
in this directory, but Unifont is GPLv2+ WITH THE FONT EMBEDDING EXCEPTION, and that exception
text is what is missing. It has to come from unifoundry.com — deliberately not paraphrased here,
because an approximated licence grant is worse than an absent one.

The four font packs in this content tree are third-party works. They are NOT covered
by COPYING.xonotic's blanket "GPL version 3 or any later version" grant: Team Xonotic
redistributes them, it does not own them, and it cannot relicense them.

Verified 2026-07-29 by reading what each pack actually ships:

  font-xolonium.pk3dir    COVERED. fonts/README.txt carries the full notice:
                          "special GPL version of the Xolonium font, intended for
                          Xonotic", GPL version 2 or any later version,
                          Copyright 2011-2020 Severin Meyer <sev.ch@web.de>.
                          Public release: https://gitlab.com/sev/xolonium

  font-unifont.pk3dir     PARTIAL. fonts/README names the work (GNU Unifont 7.0.06,
                          http://unifoundry.com/unifont.html) but carries no licence
                          text. GNU Unifont is distributed under the GPL with a font
                          embedding exception; that exception text is NOT in this tree
                          and needs adding from unifoundry.com.

  font-dejavu.pk3dir      MISSING. Ships DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf and DejaVuSansMono.ttf
                          with no notice of any kind. The DejaVu fonts are released
                          under the Bitstream Vera Fonts Copyright with the Arev Fonts
                          Copyright addition — a permissive licence, NOT the GPL, which
                          requires the copyright notice and permission notice to be
                          included in all copies. Source: https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/

  font-nimbussansl.pk3dir MISSING. Ships n019004l.pfb/.pfm/.afm with no notice. These
                          are URW++ Nimbus Sans L. Needs the URW++ notice as shipped by
                          the upstream font package.

What to do
----------

For each MISSING/PARTIAL entry, obtain the licence text from the font project itself and
add it here as FONTS.<name>. Do not paraphrase or reconstruct licence text from memory —
these are legal documents and only the authoritative copy is any use.

Nothing here blocks development. It does want closing before a public release that ships
these fonts, because two of the four are currently distributed with no notice at all, and
in the DejaVu case the licence specifically requires one.

Context: before the repo restructure this content was fetched at build time and never
committed, so the notices lived in the upstream checkout and travelled with nothing. This
file exists because that changed. See planning/repo-restructure-2026-07-29.md D1/D2 and
section 10.
